# ── XET STALL GUARD: bound stalled Xet downloads in [4/6] ────────────────────────
# nvidia/GR00T-N1.7-LIBERO is 142.79GB of 142.83GB Xet-backed (150 of 203 files, measured)
# — the largest Xet exposure of any target in this repo. Xet-backed blobs are fetched by
# the hf_xet Rust client rather than huggingface_hub's python http_get, so
# HF_HUB_DOWNLOAD_TIMEOUT does NOT apply to them; only the HF_XET_CLIENT_* knobs below do.
#
# Isaac-GR00T's uv.lock pins hf-xet==1.4.2, which carries the retry-backoff defect:
# ExponentialBackoff::from_millis(self.base_delay) uses base_delay as both the first delay
# and the per-step multiplier, so delays run 3s -> 9000s (2.5h) -> 7500h. The first retry
# after a stalled socket therefore sleeps ~2.5h and is indistinguishable from a permanent
# hang. Fixed in hf-xet 1.5.2 — 1.5.0 and 1.5.1 still carry it (checked against upstream
# source at each tag); 1.5.2 also raises the default read_timeout 120s -> 300s.
# All four names below exist in both the 1.4.x and 1.5.x binaries, so this block is not a
# no-op if an older hf_xet is resolved back in, but on the buggy versions
# RETRY_MAX_DURATION is dead config (parsed, never consulted) — shortening the retry sleep
# itself needs the version bump below.
export HF_XET_CLIENT_READ_TIMEOUT=60
export HF_XET_CLIENT_CONNECT_TIMEOUT=30
export HF_XET_CLIENT_RETRY_MAX_DURATION=120
export HF_XET_FIXED_DOWNLOAD_CONCURRENCY=8

{% if remote_grpc_endpoint %}
